# W4a — GPUDirect RDMA over the coherent C2C link (Grace-Blackwell).
# VERDICT 2026-09-03: CLOSED, no effect possible. Booted once with this overlay: NCCL still
# reports "GDR 0". Root causes, all structural on this stack: CUDA on GB10 reports
# CU_DEVICE_ATTRIBUTE_DMA_BUF_SUPPORTED=0 and GPU_DIRECT_RDMA_SUPPORTED=0 (INTEGRATED=1,
# unified memory); rdma-core 50.0 (host and image) lacks mlx5dv_reg_dmabuf_mr@MLX5_1.25;
# the stock kernel's ib_core has no ib_register_peer_memory_client, so nvidia_peermem
# cannot register. Host bounce buffers are the only NET path on this platform. Kept as a
# record; do not re-run.
# W1 (2026-09-03) showed NCCL 2.30.7 running with "GDR 0" on every ring: nvidia_peermem is
# not loaded and cuMemGdrSupport=0, so every NET message is staged through host bounce
# buffers. NCCL_NET_GDR_C2C=1 lets the NIC DMA into GPU buffers over C2C; GDR_LEVEL=SYS
# removes the PCI-distance gate; DMABUF_ENABLE=1 registers GPU memory via dma-buf.
# Engine flags = production. Rollback: ./tp4ctl restart without TP4_ENV (~22 min).
# Verdict rule: keep only if prefill 30k AND 100k >= +6% with decode within +-3%, or
# decode prose AND code >= +7% (docs/bench.md, plan decision rule).
EXTRA_DOCKER_ENV="-e NCCL_NET_GDR_C2C=1 -e NCCL_NET_GDR_LEVEL=SYS -e NCCL_DMABUF_ENABLE=1 -e NCCL_DEBUG=INFO -e NCCL_DEBUG_SUBSYS=INIT,NET -e NCCL_DEBUG_FILE=/cache/nccl-w4a-%h-%p.log"
